# The scent tree PAX carries as /bin/scent, /bin/grep (a symbolic link
# to scent) and the /bin/egrep and /bin/fgrep wrappers (px64;
# tools/mkscent builds it).
#
# scent is grep in wolf (wolffe-lang/scent, Track 15, ruling #114),
# byte-identical to GNU grep 3.12 configured --disable-perl-regexp in the
# C locale on every M1 option but the differences rulings #115-#117
# publish and the eight rows blocked upstream (scent's
# tests/divergences.json). scent is public; its source is never read
# here beyond what building it needs (scent's own rule: nobody reads
# GNU grep's source, and pax has no reason to read scent's).
#
# scent trunk at the time of px64 (2026-10-23): b6f63a4 (ct02's merge,
# scent#6, M1), pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.35 /
# lupin 0.1.56 / wolf-std 2386522e, the std the wolf 0.2.35 archive
# bundles. tools/mkscent builds it with THAT toolchain, not with
# kernel/wolf.pin's, as the lope and aspen builders build theirs (px54,
# px57), by scent's own static flags, twice, refusing two digests.
#
# The static binary depends on the libc.a it links: ct02's tools/mkscent
# in its Ubuntu 24.04 container (glibc 2.39-0ubuntu8.9) gave
# bd860457f2ff97591b7525da5f46c186feee4b8266d3f51b121866b001135d89,
# 14,846,984 bytes, twice.
SCENT_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/scent
# px64 (2026-10-23): ct02, M1: the default syntax, -E and -F on the whole M1 interface; wolf 0.2.35.
SCENT_REV=81d761d6d3b3c32f83a7b54801728088afea245a

# px82: launch trunk, 102 commits after the preceding pin.
# Codeload source archive sha256, read twice on hasu.
SCENT_SOURCE_SHA256=15f4b5261a623fe3c7470965483c63c9a30b6f908a6f274da0d0040c450da9fa
